  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bridging Phase: Hotspot prioritisation through co-creation in Semarang region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of the bilateral collaboration between Indonesia and the Netherlands, it is the ambition to further investigate a tailormade approach for the North Java / Semarang region. This is a direct collaboration with the national government of Indonesia, particularly Bappenas and PUPR (Ministry of National Development Planning, Ministry of Public Works and Housing). As such, in Phase I a Setting the Scene document is developed, investigating mutual shared objectives towards collaboration in the North Java / Semarang region, both among various institutional levels of the government of Indonesia (GoI) as well as between GoI and the government of the Netherlands (GoNL), lay groundwork by mapping relevant information on policy, socio-economic, technical, financial and institutional setup and developments, while at the same time making optimal use of existing knowledge and partnerships and finally, advice on an appropriate working method for taking next steps.In the Bridging Phase &#x2013; this assignment - local, provincial and national stakeholders will be guided in prioritising the six identified hotspots out of Phase I, narrowing them down to two hotspots for further in-depth research into potential intervention packages. The consultations will be backed by additional technical detailing on potential project intervention packages. As such, stakeholder momentum is kept, for continuation of the bilateral activities in a later stage.</narrative>
  </description>
